--- !u!114 &3621181172599023909
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 168321873214920487}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c5236d538fb060b48834286d70f34fa6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Pilar.Context::Pilar.Context.ContextNode
  _entries:
  - key: Function
    value: Main operator panel. Samples its eight push buttons - five machine commands
      and three mode selections - into one PLC symbol, and lights each button back
      from the same symbol.
  - key: Signal
    value: PanelSampler. Holds an ordered list of child components, disables their
      individual communication and exposes one aggregated FB_Panel DWORD instead.
      LateUpdate packs each child status bit into the link and unpacks control bits
      back, so the PLC addresses the whole panel through this single symbol.
  - key: BitLayout
    value: 'Verified 2026-08-20 from the live PanelSampler _components list, 8 bits
      used of 32: bit0 START, bit1 RESET, bit2 STOP, bit3 CLEAR, bit4 ABORT, bit5
      PRODUCTION, bit6 MAINTANANCE, bit7 MANUAL. StatusData carries the pressed state
      to the PLC; ControlData drives each button''s own feedback lamp at the same
      bit. Order follows the _components list - reordering it changes the PLC bit
      assignment.'
  - key: oc.plcPath
    value: MAIN.FG_System.H_ControlPanel
  - key: oc.deviceType
    value: PanelSampler
  - key: Variant
    value: This is ControlPanel variant for TwinCAT Project. PackML like control
      panel for main machine PackML state machine
  _topologySegment: 
  _topologyParent: {fileID: 0}
